You are developing a prototype called ForensiDrive.

ForensiDrive is NOT intended to be a conventional Linux desktop application.

It is a graphical control/orchestration layer designed to run on top of SystemRescue Linux when booted from a live USB/ISO.

The eventual goal is:

POWER ON
→ SystemRescue boot
→ graphical environment
→ ForensiDrive automatically starts
→ ForensiDrive becomes the primary user-facing interface

The underlying SystemRescue environment remains responsible for Linux, drivers, storage access, forensic utilities, recovery utilities, filesystem utilities, and destructive low-level operations.

Do NOT implement a custom display server, X server, Wayland compositor, kernel, window manager, or replacement Linux environment.

Instead, build the application so that it can eventually be installed into a SystemRescue filesystem such as:

/usr/local/forensidrive/

and automatically launched by SystemRescue graphical autostart.

==================================================
CURRENT DEVELOPMENT ENVIRONMENT
==================================================

The application is currently being developed directly inside a booted SystemRescue graphical environment.

Python is available.

Tkinter works.

PyQt6 is NOT installed and must NOT be used.

Use Python 3 and Tkinter.

Do not require pip packages unless absolutely unavoidable.

Prefer standard Python libraries and command-line utilities already provided by SystemRescue.

